Next, it initializes a variable to store the sign of the number (1 for positive, -1 for negative) and an index variable to iterate through the characters of the string. If the first character is a plus (+) or minus (-) sign, it updates the sign accordingly and moves the index to the next character.

Then, it iterates through the remaining characters of the string. For each character, it checks if it is a digit. If it is, it converts the digit character to its numeric value and updates the result by multiplying it by 10 and adding the digit value. It also checks if the result will exceed the integer range during this process and returns the maximum or minimum value accordingly.

If any non-digit character is found during the iteration, it returns 0.

Finally, it multiplies the result by the sign variable and returns the final value.

