Here's an example program that sorts an array of integers in ascending order using the Bubble Sort algorithm and tracks the number of comparisons made during the sorting process:

```csharp
using System;

class BubbleSort
{
    static void Main()
    {
        int[] arr = { 5, 2, 8, 1, 9, 3, 7 };

        Console.WriteLine("Original array: ");
        PrintArray(arr);

        int comparisons = BubbleSortAscending(arr);

        Console.WriteLine("Sorted array: ");
        PrintArray(arr);

        Console.WriteLine("Total comparisons: " + comparisons);
    }

    static int BubbleSortAscending(int[] arr)
    {
        int comparisons = 0;
        int n = arr.Length;

        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++)
        {
            for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++)
            {
                comparisons++; // Increment comparisons for each comparison made

                if (arr[j] > arr[j + 1])
                {
                    // Swap arr[j] and arr[j+1]
                    int temp = arr[j];
                    arr[j] = arr[j + 1];
                    arr[j + 1] = temp;
                }
            }
        }

        return comparisons;
    }

    static void PrintArray(int[] arr)
    {
        foreach (int num in arr)
        {
            Console.Write(num + " ");
        }

        Console.WriteLine();
    }
}
```

The above program defines a `BubbleSort` class with a `Main` method. In the `Main` method, an array `arr` is initialized with some values. The `BubbleSortAscending` method is then called to sort the array in ascending order and return the total number of comparisons made during the sorting process. The `PrintArray` method is used to print the elements of the array.

The `BubbleSortAscending` method implements the Bubble Sort algorithm by iterating over the array and comparing adjacent elements. If the elements are in the wrong order, they are swapped. The number of comparisons is tracked using the `comparisons` variable. The method returns the total number of comparisons made.

Finally, the sorted array and the total number of comparisons are displayed in the `Main` method.

