The `BinarySearchLastOccurrence` function performs a binary search on the array to find the last occurrence of the target element. It uses recursion and checks if the middle element is the target and if it's the last occurrence. If it's not the last occurrence, it recursively searches in the left half or right half of the array based on whether the middle element is greater than the target.

