        {
            int lastNumber = numbers[numbers.Length - 1];
            int sum = lastNumber % 2 == 0 ? lastNumber : 0;
            Array.Resize(ref numbers, numbers.Length - 1);
            return sum + SumOfEvenNumbers(numbers);
        }
    }
}
```

In the solution, the `SumOfEvenNumbers` method uses recursion to calculate the sum of even numbers in the array. It checks the last element of the array and adds it to the sum if it is even. Then, it removes the last element from the array and calls itself recursively with the updated array until the array is empty. This approach effectively sums the even numbers without using any built-in iteration constructs.

